{
  "about": "Cell pack format v1 (STR-24), the contract between genex-stream's reader and writer (crates/genex-stream/src/pack.rs, held by crates/genex-stream/tests/pack.rs) and the host's placement compiler (C-28), which must write these bytes exactly. A pack is a folder under assets/: `world` is the exact text of its world.json, and each `cells` row is one cells/<x>_<z>.cell file, its bytes as hex and what they hold as `content`. A cell body is postcard 1.x wire format: unsigned integers as LEB128 varints, signed as zigzag varints, f32 as 4 bytes little-endian, strings as a varint byte length and UTF-8, sequences as a varint count and the items, options as 0 or 1 and the value, a collider shape as its varint index in `colliderShapes` and its fields. Field order: version, cell x, cell z, terrain, nav, things, colliders, models, groups, far. A transform is translation xyz, rotation xyzw, scale xyz. world.json is compact JSON with its keys in the order shown; cells are listed ascending by x, then z; a listed cell's `fnv` is the FNV-1a 64 of its body. Paths are assets/-relative and must pass genex-core's is_safe_asset_path. Refusals are the codes below.",
